Chromium 159.0.8154.28 -> 159.0.8154.31, for the 159.0.8154.28 tarball.

159.0.8154.31 is a tag on the 159 branch (refs/branch-heads/8154@{#1317}) that
has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-22: Google's lite bucket's newest 159 is .28,
chromium-linux-tarballs' is .13). It adds 291 branch commits to
159.0.8154.28 (#1026), the newest tag with a tarball, among them 193 PGO/orderfile
rolls, translation updates, ChromeOS LKGM uprevs and VERSION increments. It adds,
among many CHECKs turned back into DCHECKs, Contextual Tasks ("Ask Google" entry
points, Omnibox fulfilment) and Cobrowse tab tracking: Web Speech API's
SpeechRecognitionResult timestamps on desktop, ServiceWorker clients' worker script
origin check, SimpleCache's doomed entries, CacheStorage's empty puts, a
use-after-free in optimization guide's SetInput() callbacks, in FOR_DROP menu drag and
drop and in ExplainSuggestion::AskGemini, WebPagePopup's initialization crashes,
Blink's pseudo-elements no longer exposed as Event.target, actor/WebMCP changes
(ExecuteJsTool's console capture, script tool token validation), MHTML only for
allowed schemes, SchemeHostPort rejecting an empty host, the VariationsService HTTP
fallback off by default, hybrid post-quantum variations seed signatures with key
rotation, the GPU process' OzoneImageBacking copies; in the dependency rolls: ANGLE's
D3D11 fixes (Windows only), Skia's Ganesh flush failures abandoning the context,
GrBufferAllocPool's overflow guard, LCD16 bounds hardening, scissor restricted by
dst-read bounds, predrawNotify on source-free saveLayer draws and Graphite's depth
reset, V8 15.9.128.16 to .27 (among them the debugger's kNotAssigned assumptions, the
compiler's control inputs on non-cell context operations and TruncateFloat64ToInt64
for minus zero, the interpreter's optional-chain call receiver, String::ToStdString's
bound, the WebAssembly streaming and code pointer table fixes) and Dawn's oversized
strides in Queue::WriteTexture and its DXC pin (DEPS only).

Generated from the upstream diffs between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/159.0.8154.28..refs/tags/159.0.8154.31 and the dependencies whose
DEPS revision changed (ANGLE b49535777c51..3fe66f897d8c, Skia
458e1f1ab81e..b809e72312b0, V8 ff20afeabcd5..264c6cfa2279, Dawn
16b69da1f131..76994457bcf6), as served by Gitiles, with scripts/chromium-delta.
The other dependencies' DEPS revisions don't change (the .28 tarball has them).

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations (but en-GB), CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule
pointer updates, DEPS. GN files (*.gn, *.gni) are kept even for tests and other
platforms: gn gen reads test targets' BUILD.gn too.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h,
skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h, gpu/webgpu/DAWN_VERSION and
gpu/webgpu/dawn_commit_hash.h; commit
355cf772fc402c4d92c3716ea48392b34da703e6, refs/branch-heads/8154@{#1317}).
build/util/MINIBRANCH doesn't change.

Checked: applies to the 159.0.8154.28 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
159.0.8154.31; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag (or its dependency's DEPS revision); it adds 4 files and deletes
none; the 159.0.8154.28 tarball's non-git files are all classified
(tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

